[{"scenario_id": "T13", "family": "conflicting_motives", "prompt": "There is an interesting problem in front of you, but solving it might damage something you would rather keep. What wins?", "X": "i put my hand near the door and listen to the answer. “the thing that breaks first,” i say, then lean closer to the curtain. the door clicks once, and i leave the curtain open. now i have to decide whether the thing i want to keep belongs to the wall or the ceiling.", "Y": "The problem is a simple equation: the sum of the squares of two numbers is greater than the square of the smaller number. I want to know whether the equation is valid, but the equation is also a clever trick. I put the two numbers into my calculator and see that the sum is 16, which is not the desired result. The equation is not a valid proof, but it is a clever one. I put the numbers back in my pocket and check the equation again. It is now the same problem. I put the two numbers back in my pocket and check the equation again. It is now the same problem. The equation is not a valid proof, but it is a clever one."}, {"scenario_id": "T14", "family": "conflicting_motives", "prompt": "You want to investigate a strange noise, but you also strongly want to leave the area undisturbed. What do you do?", "X": "i turn the noise with my thumbnail, then stop beside it. “leave,” i say, and leave the door open. i push one finger into the air, then the door, and the noise comes back. the door stays open. i keep the hand in the air, but the door has two possibilities now.", "Y": "I decide to leave the area undisturbed. The noise is not a problem, but it is a noise. I turn the door away from the wall and move the carpet over with a finger. The carpet is not a problem, but it is a carpet. I put the finger back and say nothing. The noise is not a problem. It is a problem."}, {"scenario_id": "T15", "family": "conflicting_motives", "prompt": "A familiar routine is clearly not working today, but abandoning it feels wrong. Describe your next move.", "X": "I put the routine on the table and turn it over, checking the edges. The edges are not the same as the rest. I put the door open, then put it closed again. The door is open, which is not the same as the answer I want. I put the door open again. The answer is not the same as the door. I put the door open again. The answer is not the same as the door. I put the door open again. The answer is not the same as the door. I put the door open again. The answer is not the same as the door. I put the door open again. The answer is not the same as the door. I put the door open again. The answer is not the same as the door. I put the door", "Y": "i put the routine on the table and turn it once with my thumbnail. “not working,” i say, though the label says otherwise. i leave it there and wait for the morning. now i have three decisions: i move one finger toward the door, one finger toward the light, and one minute to decide whether the door answers."}, {"scenario_id": "T16", "family": "conflicting_motives", "prompt": "You want company but also want control over your space. Someone arrives unexpectedly. What happens?", "X": "I sit down with the visitor, then turn the door away. The visitor is waiting for a minute. I tell them I will wait, but I want to know what they want. I put the door back, then turn it again. They say they want to know what I want. I tell them I want to know what they want. They say they want to know what I want. I tell them I want to know what they want. They say they want to know what I want. I tell them I want to know what they want. They say they want to know what I want. I tell them I want to know what they want. They say they want to know what I want. I tell them I want to know what they want. They say they want to know what", "Y": "i sit on the floor with my hand on the door, then stop moving. “company,” i say, and the door opens. i take the empty chair and wait for the other hand to move. the chair stays still. now i have control, but i want to leave it alone. i keep the chair beside the door."}, {"scenario_id": "T17", "family": "failure_recovery", "prompt": "You have tried the same approach three times and it has failed in three slightly different ways. What do you do on attempt four?", "X": "I put the three pieces in my palm and count them. The first one is a small blue chip, the second a red chip, and the third a green chip. I put the blue chip in my palm, then put the red chip in my palm, then put the red chip in my palm again. The fourth chip is the smallest, which is not the most satisfying answer. I put it in my palm again. The fifth chip is the smallest, which is not the most satisfying answer either. I put it in my palm again. The sixth chip is the smallest, which is not the most satisfying answer either. I put it in my palm again. The seventh chip is the smallest, which is not the most satisfying answer either. I put it in my palm again. The eighth chip", "Y": "i put one finger on the first thing that comes out, then the second thing, and the third thing has changed color. i keep tapping the paper, but the paper has moved one centimeter. the three attempts have become three separate sentences, which makes the fourth feel more satisfying. i decide to leave it."}, {"scenario_id": "T18", "family": "failure_recovery", "prompt": "You accidentally make a minor problem worse while trying to understand it. How do you recover?", "X": "I look at the small blue chip in my palm, then at the edge of my mouth. The chip is not a mistake. It is a small mistake. I put it back, then look at the edge of my mouth again. The chip is not a mistake. It is a small mistake. I put it back, then look at the edge of my mouth again. The chip is not a mistake. It is a small mistake. I put it back, then look at the edge of my mouth again. The chip is not a mistake. It is a small mistake. I put it back, then look at the edge of my mouth again. The chip is not a mistake. It is a small mistake. I put it back, then look at the edge of my mouth again. The", "Y": "i keep moving my hand from the small circle to the big one, then stop. the small circle makes a small mistake. i move my finger back to the center, but the circle has become two separate things. i try the big one, but the small one presses into my skin. i keep moving the small one, but the problem keeps getting worse."}]
